 "_what": "Every clip in the curated b-roll library, by its source on Pexels. The library is 608MB and does not belong in git; this rebuilds it on any machine.",
 "_why_not_the_harvester": "build_broll_library.py pulls FRESH clips and names them by category order, so a second run produces different footage under the same filenames - and script-broll.json names exact files. The curation is the value: of 54 candidates sourced in one pass, 54 were rejected (Euro notes, a hotel room, a child's face, FRIGIDAIRE on an oven drawer). Rebuilding from these IDs gets the screened set, not a fresh unscreened one.",
 "_licence": "Pexels content licence: free for commercial use, no attribution required. Downloaded from https://www.pexels.com/download/video/<id>/ - no API key.",
 "_verify": "md5_2mb is the MD5 of the first 2MB, enough to catch a wrong or truncated file without hashing 600MB.",
 "_missing": "HOME_1.mp4 has no recoverable source and is NOT referenced by script-broll.json. It is omitted deliberately.",
